  "conclusion": "Both horizontal normal GTK2 palette cells equal the historical SR10.4 cells at 0/225. Applying the shared press rule to the historical normal cells yields the selected GTK2 left/right pressed assets exactly at 0/225; each derived transition changes 53 pixels. This confirms the GTK2 recipe follows the common design contract for horizontal held arrows, but it is a rule-derived comparison, not a direct observation of a held horizontal arrow in the Domain/OS VM. R344 remains the valid correction for the normal-cell corner counts: 3/225 left and 1/225 right, all outside the glyph.",
  "limits": [
    "Does not replace the direct horizontal held-state capture from the SR10.4 VM.",
    "Does not provide human visual acceptance or live application reload proof.",
    "No code, theme, profile, application, or VM was modified."
  ],
  "next": "Continue I167/GTK2. When the separately owned MAME instance is gone, capture the actual horizontal held state in the canonical VM; retain live-app and human review."
